      "side": 1,
      "message": "\"Debug detach\" is a concept specific to certain TCPCs (maybe just the RAA489000?), outside of the relevant specs. I don\u0027t think it\u0027s formally documented anywhere. It has instead developed organically as a set of workarounds for weird things that happen on transition from DTS mode. I think some of those things are nondeterministic.\n\nTo validate a change like this, you\u0027d want to observe some number of transitions involving DTS of different types on real hardware. The scenarios to test should probably be informed by the history of bugs that motivated changes to the debug detach process or when it was called.",
      "revId": "ba826679c375e83c5e4453c38c02cc7e405e5a89",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5902d790_6e3df2f0",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_tc_drp_acc_trysrc_sm.c",
        "patchSetId": 5
